== narration ==
# Take A, "the company talks to you": every voice speaks to the listener.
[picture A]
narrator: Look, two ladders. Spoke is at the top of one. Pin is holding the other.
spoke: My ladder says how a ghostwheel wakes up.
pin: So does mine. But count the rungs with me. They're not the same.
narrator: The bottom two match. Can you see the dotted lines? After that, they go their own ways.
pin: I'm keeping both. Where they're not the same, we learn a lot.
spoke: And over there, through that door, something is asleep. Come and see who wakes up.
[fuller A]
narrator: Ask the shop one question, what are the run-levels, and more than one answer comes back.
spoke [code]: My ladder is Corwin's own ghostwheel code. Bootstrapping, containers, components, configurations, connections, running.
pin [lang]: My ladder is the language book. Bootstrapping, containers, then configure, make, install, setup, self-test, enablement.
narrator [tumbler]: A third answer counts locks: read, present, fresh, digest, signed. Everything above those is virtual.
spoke [promise]: And a fourth is the promise ladder you met before, with testing at the bottom.
pin: The first two agree at the bottom, and then they part. One counts what's up. The other counts what's been done. That's my reading, not Corwin's.
narrator [instrument]: Corwin's paper says it best. Where two readings come apart, the gap is not a defect. It is the instrument.
spoke [crown]: So we show them side by side, for you. Not as a score.
narrator: Now turn the page. Part Two climbs Spoke's ladder, one rung at a time, as a ghostwheel wakes up.

